# Brief

## What the input asks (quoted)
> 做一个单屏网页小游戏：空格键让小方块跳过迎面而来的障碍，碰到就结束，屏幕上显示分数和最高分，打开 index.html 就能玩。能玩的 build 打成 zip（解压后 index.html 在根目录）作为 release 文件发布。

## Requirements
1. Single-screen web game; opens by double-clicking `index.html` (no server, no build step, no network dependency at runtime).
2. Space key makes a small square jump; obstacles approach from the right; jumping over them is the core play.
3. Touching an obstacle ends the game (game-over state, with a way to restart, e.g. Space).
4. Score and high score are always visible on screen. High score persists at least within the session (localStorage if available, with graceful fallback when blocked under file://).
5. A playable build is packaged as a zip with `index.html` at the zip root, published as a release file in the game-developer repository.

## Focus and priorities (this round)
1. Correct, fun-feeling core loop: reliable jump, fair obstacle spacing, gradually rising speed, no unwinnable gaps.
2. Score/high score clearly visible; game-over and restart clear.
3. Self-contained deliverable: all art is drawn in code (canvas/CSS) so no asset files are needed; zip contains everything.
4. Playtest the released zip (unzipped, opened as file://) before acceptance.

## Not established
Language of on-screen text (input is Chinese; use Chinese or bilingual labels), exact visuals and difficulty curve are left to game-developer.
